.SH NAME
le-watch - Notify when a listener's process exits


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBle watch [port|pid] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Poll until the process behind a port (or a PID) exits, then report it —
the notify-on-exit workflow. With --timeout, give up after that long
and exit 124 (the process is still running).

.PP
Exit codes: 0 success · 1 failure · 2 usage error · 124 --timeout elapsed.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for watch

.PP
\fB-t\fP, \fB--timeout\fP=0s
	give up after this long (e.g. 30s); 0 waits forever


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBle(1)\fP


